	(text "FRANK PGA2 - two PGA2350 (RP2350B) joined by the FRANK Core2 parallel link.\n\nLINK (identical to frank_core2_proto, firmware compatible pin numbers):\n  Bus A D0..D7  master GP20..27 -> slave GP1..8,   CLK master GP28 -> 33R -> slave GP9,  VALID GP29 -> GP10\n  Bus B D0..D7  slave GP11..18 -> master GP30..37, CLK slave GP19 -> 33R -> master GP38, VALID GP20 -> GP39\n  FS GP40 -> GP21, DB_MS GP41 -> GP22, DB_SM GP23 -> GP42, master GP43 -> slave RUN\n  Place each 33R next to the DRIVING pin (R for bus A at the master, bus B at the slave).\n\nMASTER: GP0/1 UART0 (J UART M), GP2/3 I2C1 -> DS3231 RTC, GP4-7 SD, GP8 STATUS LED (LD1), GP9-11 TDA1387,\n        GP12-19 HDMI + VGA (shared, as FRANK PGA), GP44/45 UART0 <-> ESP-01, GP46 TAPE IN, USB -> USB sheet.\nSLAVE:  GP24/25 UART1 (J UART S), GP26 LED, USB -> hub port 1.  GP27-46 free.\nUSB: hub 1 (P0 master in PC mode, P1 slave, P2 -> hub 2) ; hub 2 -> 4x USB-A.\nGP47 = PSRAM CS inside PGA2350 (not used externally).\nUART NOTE: master GP0/1 (J UART M) and GP44/45 (ESP-01) are BOTH UART0 on the RP2350 - only one can use the\n           hardware UART at a time; run the other one as a PIO UART in firmware.\n\nDifferences vs Core2 proto firmware: slave PSRAM is the PGA2350 one (CS GP47, not GP0);\nmaster GP46 = TAPE IN; master status LED on GP8 (LD1); tape on FRANK PGA was GP22."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 118.11 213.36 0)
		(effects
